# Oscillations 21 — Normal modes of a three-mass chain between two walls
#
# (Goldstein, Classical Mechanics, §6.4; Taylor §11.5; Marion & Thornton ch. 12.)
# Three carts on a frictionless track are joined to each other and to two fixed
# walls by four identical springs, k = 40.0 N/m.
#
#   (a) Equal masses m = 0.250 kg. The fixed–fixed chain of N masses has
#           ω_n = 2 √(k/m) sin(nπ / (2(N + 1))),   n = 1 … N,
#       with mode shapes sin(j n π/(N + 1)), j = 1 … N. Get the frequencies from
#       eigenvalues(K, M) and compare; print the mode shapes.
#   (b) Make the middle cart heavier, m₂ = 0.500 kg (the outer ones stay 0.250 kg).
#       The antisymmetric mode (middle cart at rest) keeps ω = √(2k/m); the two
#       symmetric ones (x₁ = x₃) solve m m₂ ω⁴ − 2k(m + m₂) ω² + 2k² = 0.
#       Find the three frequencies and check that the mode shapes are M-orthogonal,
#       v_iᵀ M v_j = 0.
#   (c) Pull cart 1 aside by 2.00 cm and release everything from rest. Project the
#       start onto the modes (q_n = v_nᵀ M x₀ / v_nᵀ M v_n), then integrate the
#       equations of motion for 5 s and compare x₁(5 s) with the modal sum
#       Σ q_n v_n1 cos(ω_n t). The energy in each mode, ½ ω_n² q_n² v_nᵀ M v_n, must
#       add up to the ½ x₀ᵀ K x₀ = k x₀² stored at the start (two springs stretched).

k = 40.0 N/m
m = 0.250 kg

# (a) equal masses
K = [[2k, -k, 0], [-k, 2k, -k], [0, -k, 2k]]
M = identity(3) m
ω2 = eigenvalues(K, M)
# (a loop `for n from 1 to 3 … ω2[n]` is refused: vector indexes must be fixed numbers; FRICTION O10)
print "equal masses, mode 1:", √(ω2[1]) to 6 digits, "vs", 2 √(k / m) sin(π / 8) to 6 digits
print "equal masses, mode 2:", √(ω2[2]) to 6 digits, "vs", 2 √(k / m) sin(2π / 8) to 6 digits
print "equal masses, mode 3:", √(ω2[3]) to 6 digits, "vs", 2 √(k / m) sin(3π / 8) to 6 digits
V = eigenvectors(K, M)
print "mode shapes (columns):", V

# (b) a heavy middle cart
m2 = 0.500 kg
Mh = [[m, 0, 0], [0, m2, 0], [0, 0, m]]
λ = eigenvalues(K, Mh)
ω_1 = √(λ[1])
ω_2 = √(λ[2])
ω_3 = √(λ[3])
print "heavy middle, slow mode:", ω_1 to 6 digits
sym = 2k (m + m2)
# (`2 m m2` here was 2 metres × m × m2: only a warning, and a number in kg^(1/2)/(m^(1/2) s) printed; FRICTION O11)
print "  quadratic for the symmetric modes:", √((sym - √(sym² - 8 k² m m2)) / (2*m m2)) to 6 digits, √((sym + √(sym² - 8 k² m m2)) / (2*m m2)) to 6 digits
print "heavy middle, middle mode:", ω_2 to 6 digits, " (antisymmetric, √(2k/m) =", √(2k / m) to 6 digits, ")"
print "heavy middle, fast mode:", ω_3 to 6 digits
W = eigenvectors(K, Mh)
v1 = <W[1, 1], W[2, 1], W[3, 1]>
v2 = <W[1, 2], W[2, 2], W[3, 2]>
v3 = <W[1, 3], W[2, 3], W[3, 3]>
print "M-orthogonality v1·Mv2, v1·Mv3, v2·Mv3:", v1 · (Mh v2), v1 · (Mh v3), v2 · (Mh v3)

# (c) release cart 1 from 2.00 cm
x0 = <2.00, 0, 0> cm
q1 = v1 · (Mh x0) / (v1 · (Mh v1))
q2 = v2 · (Mh x0) / (v2 · (Mh v2))
q3 = v3 · (Mh x0) / (v3 · (Mh v3))
print "modal amplitudes:", q1 to 6 digits, q2 to 6 digits, q3 to 6 digits

solve m x1'' = -k x1 + k (x2 - x1),
      m2 x2'' = -k (x2 - x1) + k (x3 - x2),
      m x3'' = -k (x3 - x2) - k x3
  with x1(0) = 2.00 cm, x2(0) = 0 cm, x3(0) = 0 cm,
       x1'(0) = 0 m/s, x2'(0) = 0 m/s, x3'(0) = 0 m/s
  for t from 0 s to 5 s

modal_x1(t) = q1 v1.x cos(ω_1 t) + q2 v2.x cos(ω_2 t) + q3 v3.x cos(ω_3 t)
print "x1(5 s), ODE vs modal sum:", x1(5 s) in cm to 6 digits, modal_x1(5 s) in cm to 6 digits
print "x3(5 s), ODE:", x3(5 s) in cm to 6 digits

E1 = ½ ω_1² q1² (v1 · (Mh v1))
E2 = ½ ω_2² q2² (v2 · (Mh v2))
E3 = ½ ω_3² q3² (v3 · (Mh v3))
print "mode energies:", E1 in mJ to 6 digits, E2 in mJ to 6 digits, E3 in mJ to 6 digits
print "sum vs ½ x₀ᵀ K x₀:", (E1 + E2 + E3) in mJ to 6 digits, (½ x0 · (K x0)) in mJ to 6 digits
